      "mentions": 18,
      "title": {
        "en": "Lengthy lines despite walk-in accessibility"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Visitors emphasize that waiting times at this walk-in clinic can be substantial, with multiple owners waiting anywhere from two to five hours to be seen. Although several clients note that arriving an hour before opening shortens the wait, others find the long hours exhausting despite the good care received inside."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "staff",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 17,
      "title": {
        "en": "Dedicated clinicians and attentive technicians"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents speak warmly of the medical staff, especially Dr. Anna Parham and technician Michael, describing them as patient, informative, and genuinely caring with animals. Clients note that doctors take ample time during exams to explain diagnoses and discuss preventive steps without rushing through questions."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "prices",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 12,
      "title": {
        "en": "Unbeatable low rates for basic visits"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Reviewers consistently applaud the clinic's budget-friendly fee structure, noting office visits under twenty dollars alongside low-cost vaccinations and basic health certificates. Clients view the affordable pricing as a vital community resource for maintaining routine pet healthcare without excessive bills."
      }
    }
  ],
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "What is the best way to minimize waiting time?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "Pet owners recommend arriving at least 30 to 60 minutes prior to opening, as lines form early outside for walk-in slots."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "What services are provided at the Holcombe location?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "The clinic primarily provides preventive care, including routine vaccinations, low-cost office exams, travel certificates, and parasite testing."
      },
      "basis": "reviews"
    },
    {
      "q": {
        "en": "Can appointments be booked ahead of time?"
      },
      "a": {
        "en": "No, the facility operates strictly on a first-come, first-served basis for walk-ins rather than scheduled appointments."
      },
      "basis": "both"
    }
